Base2300 originated in an earlier private project by the same author and was
extracted into this standalone repository. The original project is not
published; this repository is the reference source for the format.

The standalone implementation is distributed under the MIT license (LICENSE).
The Joyo Kanji data in src/base2200Alphabet.ts derives from Unicode 17.0.0
Unihan kJoyoKanji=2010 and retains the Unicode-3.0 license, reproduced in
licenses/unicode-3.0.txt. That notice was copied unchanged from the source
project. The data's code-point ordering is part of the wire format.

Unicode source:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unicode-org/unicodetools/main/unicodetools/data/ucd/17.0.0/Unihan/kJoyoKanji.txt
Property definition: https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/#kJoyoKanji
Current upstream license: https://www.unicode.org/license.txt

No backend daemon, LLM weights, external reading dictionary or KANJIDIC2 data
is distributed by this package. No Unishox, SCSU, Smaz or qntm codec source has
been incorporated into the library.

Benchmark-only snapshots of qntm's Base2048 and Base32768 are included under
bench/vendor, under their original MIT licenses. They are not runtime library
dependencies or part of the npm package. Their source URLs, snapshot hashes,
license notices and known-answer checks are recorded in bench/vendor/README.md.
